Welcome crawlers to the sixth Dungeon Crawler Carl book recap where I'll be covering the Eye of the Bedlam Bride chapter by chapter and don't worry there are no spoilers outside of what happens inside this book. And 
finally, if you appreciate well-crafted book summaries like this, make sure to like and subscribe to Manitous for more content in the future. All right, let's get started with chapter one. In a flashback to Mordecai's 
time as a crawler, his party becomes trapped on the collapsing 10th floor and needs god-tier lightning to open stairwell. Their manager, who is Odette, had privately bribed Wuxian Jinx to drive her sponsored storm 
goddess Thedola to the door. But Wuxian repeatedly increases her price and threatens to kill the party. Odette convinces the party member Chaco to carry out an alternative plan forcing an involuntary summon that kills 
Mordecai's brother and manifests Thedola inside a containment shell allowing Mordecai to kill the goddess and open the stairwell. Realizing Odette deliberately influenced Chaco to sacrifice his brother, Mordecai vows to 
escape and kill her. Carl and Donut arrive on the eighth floor, the ghosts of Earth. The floor is a replica of Earth in December of the previous year split into 293 regions. The world is a ghost replay where living 
people and animals are somewhat phantoms that can't be interacted with but all non-biological items retain their mass and can be used or destroyed freely though anything looted from this floor will turn to dust at its 
collapse. Each region is also seeded with monsters from local folklore. Crawlers receive flags that can transform weakened monsters into reusable taggy cards which will reform their squads and eventually be used in 
card-based battles during phase two which starts in 14 days. Donut chooses the psychic class for this floor which gains her a new mapping ability in addition to the brain freeze, bad attitude, and why are you hitting 
yourself abilities. In the safe room, Mordecai, now a cyclops after the floor change, notices that Samantha is gaining abilities she should not possess and warns Carl that they need to find out exactly what is going on 
with her. Carl and Donut open their butcher's masquerade rewards, where Donut receives the enchanted fur brush of the colastic, giving her a boost of plus 10% constitution, a cosmic buff potion that raises a random stat 
by 10, she gets dexterity, a skill potion boosting her love vampire skill to level six, so it now auto casts, and a team buff spellbook called rigorous. She also picks up a mercenary coupon worth 100,000 gold at Meat 
Shields, the floor's mercenary market. Carl's a big prize is the tone book for legionnaires of the damned, a spell that animates discarded weapons and armor, making it a perfect addition to combine with Donut's laundry 
day spell. Carl opens his remaining rewards, which includes a free town upgrade coupon, a crafting table kit, an automaton building kit, and a magical tattoo set like the one used by Signus' tortoise Edgar. His greatest 
reward is the scavenger's daughter patch, which strengthens his jacket and grants soul reaper, allowing him to collect soul essence from melee kills and release it when full into one single powerful attack. It also 
grants the mysterious bone key, which can be used once to open any lock, but will destroy his jacket and permanently remove a random bone from his body. Carl also equips the enchanted nipple ring of the defiler, which 
identifies nearby religious affiliations, lets him destroy church shrines without reprisal, adds 25% bonus damage against clerics, and grants the black nimbus spell. Meanwhile, Katia worries about Brittany, whose burned 
face from the last floor hasn't healed. Donut is horrified when the system generated squad flag for the royal court of Princess Donut appears as a pair of heart-covered boxer shorts. Carl then sets traps around the 
nearby stairwell, guarding it against any crawler outside their guild, and he, Donut, and Samantha begin scouting Old Havana. The first major enemy they encounter is a level 55 Taino guardian resembling a giant bearded 
man in a red beret riding a wolf-like body. Donut and Carl kill it, and the creature drops a very rare combo card which can temporarily fuse two summoned monsters. As they examine the reward, three other crawlers 
approach from the coast. The approaching crawlers are Paz, Anton, and a level 47 Havana brown cat girl nun named Sister Inez. Paz and Anton worship the god Ogun, making them immune to charm effects. Donut immediately 
dislikes Sister Inez because of her cat girl class, and the newcomers are frightened because of a previous broadcast clip where Donut was making threats against Havana browns. Despite their distrust, Carl pushes for 
cooperation. Sister Inez proposes that the two groups help one another capture their first squad members. Their target is a group of monk seals on a nearby beach, one of which nearly killed Anton already. The group 
discovers that the monk seals practice a martial art called Caribbean kung fu, and examining them triggers a quest called The Chowder Wars, which requires Carl to eventually side with either the monk seals or the rival 
red minicero's land crabs. They target Yago, a level 70 monk seal, and while they attack it, Carl plants the flag into it once its health falls below 5%, turning Yago into a tag card. Carl gives the card to Sister Inez 
as agreed, and when another seal named Geraldo attacks, the group repeats the process to capture him for Carl and Donut's deck. After capturing Geraldo, the two groups begin to head toward a safe room. Zev tells Carl 
and Donut that they have been booked on Shadow Boxer, a documentary style program owned by one of Carl's sponsors, and the Carl's segment will focus on his teenage years without a guardian. She also warns them about an 
upcoming Faction Wars pre-production meeting. Along the way, they kill a swarm of weak duendes. The melee kills fill Carl's soul essence bar for the first time and unlocks the daughter's kiss, which will massively 
strengthen his next melee attack. Each use of this ability will increase the amount of soul essence the bar can hold and increase the power of the following strike. The groups reach the safe room and agree to work 
together again, although Donut remains deeply suspicious of Sister Inez. During the recap, the card combat system that will begin in phase two is explained further. Decks use totem, utility, snare, mystic, and special 
cards with six active totems required for each battle. During a card battle, the squad leader will control the cards but loses access to their magic and inventory, leaving the rest of the squad responsible for 
protecting them. Killing a nether card-carrying squad allows the winner to take its cards, and safe rooms now contain paid practice arenas. Samantha then reports that she found a pulpmancer who could help her gain a 
body, but that the mage ate her because that mage, as it turns out, is She Maria, the bedlam bride, a unique spider demigoddess whose attacks include permanent insanity and blindness. Rather than abandoning Samantha, 
Carl decides She Maria could become a powerful squad totem for their deck. Carl, Donut, and use the mock battle arena to practice with the card combat system. They learn that the four drawn cards float in front of the 
squad leader. Cards can only be discarded every 30 seconds, and utility cards can be used to strengthen a summon totem. Because their only totem drawl though is only an uncommon, he can hold two utility effects while 
rarer monsters will be able to carry more. A nearby park turns out to be a cemetery and entering it triggers a quest to cure the residents who have been transformed into ravenous undead spirits. In the cemetery gates 
lock behind the group preventing their escape. The party battles increasingly large waves of level 30 Gomids. Paz's holy armor draws their attacks while sister Innes, Anton, Donut, Carl, and fight toward a safe room. 
They barely make it inside, but the level 130 city boss opens the safe room door and walks in after them. The boss is Asujano, the lord of smallpox, a former god whose presence corrupted the Gomids. Because safe room 
protections prevent him from fighting, he asks Paz to repair his shrine so he can leave and the town can be restored. The group can either repair the shrine or kill every corrupted resident. Carl and Anton attempt to 
weaken and flag him, but sister Innes objects to killing a former god and Asujano escapes to regenerate before reaching 5% health. Carl and Donut open the remaining fan boxes and Donut receives the bard's golden throat 
microphone, which improves and amplifies her bard spell songs. While Carl receives a very rare snare card called hobbled, which reduces an enemy's totem remaining summon time by 90%. Katia, Bautista, and Louie arrive to 
exchange cards and information. Zev then announces that Carl and Donut's shadow boxer interview begins in a few minutes. Carl and Donut transfer to the underwater shadow boxer studio where the liaison is Harbinger, a 
powerful caprid from the plenty. Carl recognizes him as the sponsor who previously helped Maggie Mae send Skull Empire orcs after him while Quasar is furious that Zev failed to warn him that Harbinger would be present. 
The host is Rosetta, a former crawler and game guide who wrote the ninth edition of the Dungeon Anarchist Cookbook and created many of the explosive recipes Carl uses. Her program focuses on raw interviews about life 
before the collapse. Donut's segment begins pleasantly with Rosetta asking her about how shows such as Gossip Girl and Gilmore Girls influenced her. Rosetta then turns to Carl, displays a wedding photograph of his 
parents, and opens his interview by asking about his dead mother. Rosetta forces Carl to recount his 15th birthday when his mother poisoned his father and hanged herself in the basement. His father survived but 
abandoned him months later, leaving Carl at a boys ranch until he turned 18. Carl also describes lying during the police investigation because he desperately wanted an adult to pay attention to him. Rosetta reveals that 
an arrest warrant was later issued for his father for child abandonment, though it was never enforced. Carl notices that several photographs and video clips contain deliberate errors and realizes Rosetta is sending him 
a hidden message through references to milk, potatoes, and root vegetables. The wording matches an exchange between cookbook author Milk and Rosetta, directing him information about the Tolarin root he had received 
previously. Harbinger recognizes some sort of deception is going on, abruptly ends the interview, bans Rosetta from future crawler appearances, and declares that he intends to try and remove Carl and the Capered Sponsor 
from the crawl. Back in the safe room, Carl equips Bomos armor with seeker smoke missiles and anti-undead stun bombs to try and reach Osahonos temple when the cemetery opens at sundown. Donut uses the bard's golden 
throat to raise the party's dexterity by 50%, but she fails to maintain the song and becomes temporarily muted. Carl then captures a rare donkey-headed splitter gomid, resulting in a nuke totem card named Skyler Spinach 
that splits into increasingly dangerous pieces when killed. Inside the temple, Asahano summons the Sun of Reawakening, a flaming ruby skull needed to restore his shrine. Before they can begin, Ogan gives Paz and Anton a 
competing order to repair his shrine instead. Anton touching Ogan's shrine triggers a boss battle and reveals a celestial thorn room containing several competing shrines, each offering different abilities and divine 
consequences, and choosing between them could permanently alter the dungeon. Katya privately urges Carl to restore Yamaya, claiming it is the only way to save both herself and Donut. Trusting her warning, Carl commits 
the group to rebuilding Yamaya's blue obelisk instead of serving Ogan or Asahano. While the others assemble the shrine, Carl combines the legionnaires of the damn spell with Bomo's scrap heap breastplate, creating a 
storm of animated metal that devastates Asahano. Now weakened, Carl flags and captures him as a totem. Yamaya reascends, curing the gomids and converting the safe room into a club vanquisher entrance. However, Carl 
contracts slug pox, and as he scrambles to get everyone to the door, Ogan appears as a level 250 invulnerable god and punishes Paz and Anton for failing to restore his shrine. He makes Paz's bleeding permanently 
unhealable and kills Anton by crushing his head. Carl's standing with Emberus is the only reason Ogan doesn't kill him as well. As Paz's health continues to drain, he warns Carl that Sister Inez's Havana brown race 
grants Toxoplasma a passive ability that causes nearby people to want to protect her and forget their own suspicions. He reveals that she was known as the Reaper of Havana and imprisoned for poisoning every nun in her 
convent, though he insists she has behaved better inside the dungeon. Donut wants to kill Sister Inez before she can manipulate anyone, but Carl refuses to execute her for what she might do. Sister Inez then uses a flag 
on the dying pause, capturing him as a totem for her deck instead of allowing him to die. Then Yemaya, goddess of rivers, and Elethia, goddess of childbirth and female pain, show up and reward the group. Yemaya gives 
Donut a mythical mystic card called the thief, which can steal a card from an opposing player, teleports Bomo to the ninth floor to reunite with the sledge, and tells Carl to see a proper healer for his slug pox. 
Elethia grants the group protection from spiritual possession, improved healing, and additional constitution. She also disguises a private communication channel as a fake spider-killing quest and secretly offers Carl a 
bargain. If Carl helps Elethia and her sponsor, Waxine Jinx, claim the celestial throne, she promises to protect Carl, Donut, and Katia through the 12th floor and provide them with a possible exit. Her first requirement 
is for them to make Odette their Faction Wars adjutant. Carl accepts and Sister Inez loots Anton's body before silently leaving for the cemetery. Carl enters Club Vanquisher to cure his slug pox and meets Pater Cole, a 
high cleric of Empress. During a private religious ritual where he washes Carl's feet, Carl realizes Pater Cole is actually the dungeon AI using the NPC body to communicate without being overheard. The AI reminds Carl 
of his quests to discover who killed Empress's son, Garin, and to kill Helak before the 12th floor. Reveals that Katia's crossbow and Donut's oak bracelet each contained part of the solution, but both require the Apito 
Memorial Crystal carried by another crawler. The crystal is especially suspicious because Memorial Crystals are only created when a god dies, and Apito is supposedly still alive. Carl is cured and receives the Martyr's 
Path Boon, which tracks every outdoor step he takes, grants additional strength, and releases fire onto those steps when his health reaches below 5%. Back in the safe room, Katia tells Carl that she must explain the 
dangerous situation in regards to her having worn the crown of the Sepsis Katia opens the Engaged Locks Box of the Night Worm, which contains the Orchid of Athilia's Grace. If eaten at 1% health, the orchid will render 
her unconscious and then grant one of three boons: either triple constitution, immediate transfer to the 12th floor as a protected celestial attendant, or a return to her original race followed by pregnancy and removal 
to the Kinder facility outside of the dungeon. Two of the box's three seals are already broken because Katia killed Ava and helped kill Imogen. To help the final seal, she must enter the Guild of Suffering and complete 
an assassination. Athilia Athilia and her sponsor, Waxing Jinx, want Katia to choose the celestial attendant option and have promised to protect her. The assassination target is Astrid, the level 125 Bloodlust Sprite 
who serves as the Desperado Club's assistant manager and owns the Naughty Boys Employment Agency. With 8 days remaining before phase two, Carl and Donut continue collecting cards while on moving towards Samantha and 
searching for a Desperado Club. Donut admits that she messaged and threatened Sister Inez over the pause card, causing the nun to block her and making a peaceful reunion unlikely. Zev reports that Odette has reached 
Earth orbit and wants Carl and Donut on her show. Odette also intends to ask publicly to become their Faction Wars adjunct, which matches Ilthilia's instructions. Inside the safe room, Carl discovers that Mordecai has 
secretly used some of their money to hire five NPC attendants, including the children Ruby, the Bear Clubs, and Skarn. The arrangement protects them by filling Mordecai's available attendant slots, although Carl is 
surprised. Mordecai refused to apologize for using the money to keep the children safe. Zev privately advises Carl not to choose Odette as adjunct. The role acts as a natural referee and commentator with open 
communication to other teams, and Zev fears that Odette's communication to Waxine and Mordecai's hatred of her could endanger the children Mordecai is trying to protect. Carl still believes he must select her to 
preserve Ilthilia's promise. At the Faction Wars pre-production meeting, Carl and Donut meet the other warlords, including Prince Stalwart, Rishi of the Blood Sultanate, Empress Donatia, Epitome Tag, the Operative 
Collective, the Reavers, and the Lemnic Sorceran. The meeting is interrupted when Epitome Tag's mother, who turns out to be the changeling Juicebox in disguise, decapitates the Madness representative and takes his seat. 
Juicebox asks Carl and Donut to propose a 10th Faction Wars team made entirely of NPCs, granting them full voting rights, protection, and regeneration. Carl submits the proposal, but Prince Stalwart blocks the vote 
before Juicebox detonates a hobgoblin pus bomb and throws the whole meeting into chaos. Rishi offers a compromise in which unaffiliated NPCs receive a protected safe zone if Juicebox ends her attacks, but the meeting 
concludes without a final decision. Back at the Desperado Club, Carl, Katia, and the others begin planning Astrid's assassination. Florence also gives Donut Uzi Jesus, a level 140 unique undead totem card with ranged 
attacks, healing abilities, and a possible resurrection skill. Carl enters the Penis Parade strip club to find Damascus steel who carries the same spider web Guild of Suffering tattoo as him. Damascus agrees to guide 
him through a hidden portal into the Guild. Upon entering, the AI delivers a long speech about how oppressed people are usually destroyed when they fight back, but they must resist anyways. Through the Guild of 
Suffering, Carl tells Katia he has gained the ability to see hidden doors, passages, drug dens, and service tunnels throughout the Desperado club and plans to use these routes to separate Astrid from her guards. Donut 
has her flawless jeweler's gem installed in a new tiara creating the enchanted tiara of the Inebriated Dragonfly which reduces potion cool-downs by 50%, grants intelligence and poison protection, removes drunkenness, 
and provides a level 10 hover ability. While continuing on their way to find and rescue Samantha, they encounter the red Manicero's land crabs migrating toward the ocean for a surprise attack on the monk seals. Carl 
identifies a level 70 warrior named Raul meditating on a truck and decides to try and capture him for their deck. Carl and Donut trap Raul inside the truck, attack him, and plant a flag transforming him into their fifth 
totem card. While waiting for the migration to pass, Carl researches She Maria. The Bedlam Bride is a spider demigoddess specializing in illusion, trickery, permanent insanity, and permanent blindness. Mordecai prepares 
liquid therapy potions to protect the Guild while Carl notices that She Maria possesses no listed spell capable of completing Samantha's body and is almost certainly lying to her. The Chowder War quest updates. Sister 
Inez has allied with the monk heels and warned them of the crab's sneak attack. So, the crab's ambush will likely become a slaughter unless Carl decides to intervene. Carl and Donut reach the web-covered territory of 
She Maria, a level 140 city boss. Samantha, still trapped inside her, relays her delusional master plan to get a body, adventure with them, have a doomed affair with Louie, host a bachelorette party, find and marry her 
missing king, and then kill her mother. Carl knows She Maria has no spell that can actually animate Donut's flesh golem, so Carl offers the spider a deal. He'll help her reach Laracna's if she lets herself be turned 
into a totem card and doesn't harm anyone. She Maria agrees, but hints that Carl has cracks that can be infiltrated from the thing growing inside of him. After capturing She Maria as the squad's sixth totem, Carl orders 
Donut to never trust her or summon her outside of combat. They also hide the fact that Laracna's was flooded since the pulpmancer Samantha needs may already be dead. The group collects a very rare damnation snare card, 
which forces an expired totem into the discard pile, and the mythic glow-up card, which permanently rewrites a card to preserve its current buffs. Carl also learns that filling up the daughter's kiss with multiple 
members of the same species creates a purer, more powerful charge. Katya has now gone silent while scouting the Desperado Club, and Bautista's claim that she is merely sleeping alarms Carl. They then hear a new 
announcement explaining how phase three will work, where squads will be placed directly in one another's path, and allow the limited number of keys to the next floor to be fought over, intentionally forcing crawlers to 
kill each other. Carl begins considering his new one-time mysterious bone key ability as a possible way around the system. Amani tells Carl that Katya used drugs from a self-service den inside the Desperado Club and 
that the effect has left her unconscious inside a recreated memory and Imani suspects that Bautista is hiding her growing addiction. Carl and Donut test their now completed 18-card deck in the arena. Their six totems 
are Geraldo, Asujano, Skyler Spinach, Uzi Jesus, Raul, and She Maria. During the supposedly safe simulation, however, She Maria opens her fifth eye and reaches into Carl's mind planting the thought, "It's the river in 
my mind." Repeated arena practice exposes the totems' personalities and weaknesses. Asujano tries to sabotage Donut, Raul and Geraldo attack each other, Uzi Jesus frequently ignores orders and lies about his abilities, 
and She Maria is sadistic but extraordinarily fast and powerful. However, in their first true practice deck versus deck challenge, Donut is killed inside the simulation leading Carl to conclude that rapid execution and 
obedience matter more than a deck's raw power and decides that they must continue training more before phase two. With 6 hours until phase two, Carl and Donut find Katia violently ill from treatment for four separate 
drug addictions. The worst is Glory Bound, a hallucinogen that traps her inside recreated memories. Her stats and skills have already been permanently damaged and she will remain vulnerable to addictive effects. 
Mordecai suggests that the strategically safest choice is to let Katia destroy herself since the crown will eventually force either Katia or Donut to die. Carl, however, refuses to abandon her and Mordecai agrees to 
help delay the hallucinogens until her squad obtains a key. Killing Astrid is now more urgent than ever since completing the contract will open Katia's celestial box and provide the orchard required for Katia's chosen 
boon. Imani applies temporary buffs and a final treatment patch and Katia, Carl, and the others move forward with their assassination plan. Carl uses the Guild of Suffering Passages to prepare a hidden quarter for 
Astrid's ambush. Katia's scouting shows that Astrid has 150 intelligence, lethal cardiovascular spells, a cosmic sense that detects divine and demonic beings, and the ability to summon up to 15 guards instantly. Carl 
places two-part teleport traps throughout the hallway to remove any guards she calls. He also disarms several existing traps and reinforces a nearby sealed room containing 15 extremely dangerous red tagged monsters 
fearing the battle could accidentally release them. As they prepare, Katia struggles with guilt over killing Astrid who has done nothing to them. Carl reminds her that she did not choose the contract and that he refuses 
to give up on her. Samantha creates a disturbance to lure Astrid, but instead breaches the nothing and releases Minch, a level 225 feral demon seeking revenge for Samantha's earlier insults. Astrid senses the demon and 
avoids Carl's traps destroying the original assassination plan. The club erupts into chaos as Minch attacks. Crawlers panic and Astrid releases the sealed Vorpals to fight the demon. Carl's traps remove several guards 
and his explosives eventually strike Astrid leaving her badly injured. Astrid reveals that the Night Worm who ordered the assassination is her husband, Ahmed, meaning he placed the contract on his own wife. Katia 
attacks in a transformed metallic body while Carl tears off Astrid's wings to prevent her from using her spells. Katia's totem kills Astrid completing the contract while Carl helps make the attack appear to have been 
committed by a monster rather than crawlers. The Night Worm confirms Astrid's death and Katia receives the Orchard of Athalia's Grace. Mordecai explains that the released Vorpals are celestial guards converted into 
living bombs that grow stronger near demons and will explode if they believe they are losing. Carl attempts to evacuate the Desperado Club's NPC workers while Minch hunts Samantha. His spider automatons and holy water 
bombs injure the demon but cannot kill her. The war poles eventually swarm Minch and destroy her themselves. Katia refuses to eat the orchid until reaching the ninth floor because doing so would abandon her squad. On 
the club's upper floor, Damascus and the other male strippers mourn Astrid, unaware that Carl and Katia had been the ones that killed her. Damascus reveals that Astrid was his mother and the night worm is his father. He 
and Anaconda were former crawlers who became part of the Desperado Club and Astrid's death means that the dancers may be reassigned to Loracco's or forced to fight in faction wars. Carl uses Donut's 100,000 gold meat 
shield coupon to hire the entire dance crew for two floors, protecting 13 dancers, a skeleton DJ, and Bucket Boy as guild mercenaries. Damascus and Anaconda then leave to confront their father. Carl realizes that many 
club workers are not generated NPCs but indentured former crawlers are naturals, reinforcing the cookbook suggestion that dungeon worlds are reused and layered over previous inhabitants. On Odette's show, Carl learns 
that the Desperado Club evacuation dumped several trapped faction wars of officials into the flooded lower level where sharks ate them. Several factions demand punishment but Carl argues that he merely returned the 
trapped participants to the game. Odette reveals rejected emergency proposals submitted by Empress Donatia, which include deleting the Loracco's NPCs, excluding crawlers from faction wars, and removing Carl and Donut 
entirely. Donut is furious that her former sponsor secretly attempted to destroy them. Odette explains that an adjutant accompanies a warlord as an invulnerable referee, rules expert, communicator, and daily 
commentator. However, she then announces that she cannot take the role herself. Odette reveals that she is entering the dungeon as the sponsor of the resurrected vulture goddess, Nekhbet, and will compete for the 
celestial throne. She presents three alternative adjutant candidates to Carl and Donut: Ripper Wonton, an interviewer they had met previously, Drik, a dream elf secretly controlled by a valky worm, and Baroness Victory, 
a skull empire attorney and judge who is also the deceased queen's half-sister. Baroness Victory promises not to hold Carl responsible for her sister's death, and Carl chooses her as their adjutant. Phase two then 
begins with a surprise. Only the squad leader will be transferred to the chosen chamber and will fight the first opponent. Donut panics about going alone, but Carl reassures her before she faces an easy level 40 
opponent named Robert the Human. While Donut fights, Odette privately explains her history to Carl. She was a crawler who later became Mordecai's manager and made an illegal arrangement with Waxine to manipulate his 
run. When Waxine increased her price, Odette broke the deal leading to Mordecai's brother's death. Now Odette plans to enter the dungeon as Nekhbet to kill Waxine even if it costs her life and help end the planetary 
harvesting system that powers the crawl. Carl transfers to Donut's location in the Florida Keys, where the destination system is malfunctioning and sending crawlers to incorrect areas. To earn the region's key, Carl and 
Donut must collect nine tokens from card-carrying monsters before facing the final keymaster. Squads have been scattered across memory recreations of places connected to their lives, and Ellie warns everyone not to be 
manipulated by ghost versions of their loved ones. Their first opponent is a level 40 babab boom in a parking lot. Carl kills it immediately with a hob lobber earning their first number token and another fleet card. 
Donut identifies a line of red dots leading towards the distant key location and they trek onward. Carl and Donut quickly collect their first several tokens. The sixth opponent, a reef explorer protected by four 
swordfish, is strong enough to require one of Donut's new creations, Lazarus a bang bang, a unique level 140 fusion of Asahano and Uzi Jesus permanently created with the combo and glow up cards. Lazarus a bang bang uses 
a bazooka that produces random effects, this time releasing metal beetles that devour the swordfish. They then discover the key rest atop a roughly 700 ft mound of earth taken from their original intended location, now 
slowly eroding into the ocean. With six tokens collected and Carl's soul essence bar nearly full, they return to the safe room to quickly rest before the final push. Inside the safe room, Donut admits that the card 
system has made her understand how quickly they could lose their friends or one another. She confesses that after Odette's show, she feared she might never see Carl again. Carl comforts her and they choose to sleep 
normally for the night rather than use the magical bed. Carl receives five scrolls of built trench while Donut opens the filthy little crawlers book of voodoo. Nearly every crawler has received a copy allowing owners 
who have met to leave permanently written messages for each other. By morning, the 700 ft mound of earth has become more unstable. At the top of the mound, the environment is a recreation of Dallas County, Iowa. The 
ninth token appears to be guarded by a spiked ogre inside an enormous turkey barn. begins slaughtering what seems to be ordinary animals, but one turkey suddenly knocks him unconscious and reveals itself to be the true 
deck master. The ogre activates at the same time, forcing Carl and Donut into a coordinated two-on-one card battle amongst thousands of hostile turkeys. The opponents are Tom, a turkey shaman, and Sharp Elbows, a spiked 
ogre necromancer. They flood the barn with summoned guards, hostile turkeys, anti-magic effects, and undead birds while heat lamps prematurely detonate Carl's explosives. Carl steals one of their cards and releases his 
fully charged Daughter's Kiss, killing Tom. Sharp Elbows then impales Carl on her venomous spikes, poking out both of his eyes. Speaking in She Maria's voice, the ogre repeats the spider's references to hunger and the 
river in Carl's mind. Raul saves the day by decapitating her, allowing Carl to heal and recover the dead bodies and tokens they carried. As the eroding cliff carries the entire turkey barn into the ocean, Donut helps 
them escape with her puddle jump ability moments before Carl passes out. Carl awakens with all nine tokens and both enemy decks secured. Donut reorganizes their cards and adds the golden combo, a reusable unique card 
capable of repeatedly fusing different totems rather than being consumed after one use. Donut begins acting unnaturally calm and suggests facing the final boss alone or abandoning the key altogether. Carl realizes she 
is trying to protect him from the final boss arena that lies ahead. The arena consists of a deteriorating trailer and junkyard assembled from Carl's childhood memories. The vending machine requires all nine tokens to 
begin the fight and warns that leaving afterward would require nine more, though no additional tokens exist. Carl recognizes his father's 1965 Harley Davidson. The fight will not begin for 42 minutes and understanding 
that the AI wants him to witness something personal, Carl asks Donut to wait outside as he enters the trailer alone. Inside, Carl sees a real-time recording of his estranged father dying in a hospital bed 12 years after 
abandoning him. He also discovers Asher, a young half whose existence had been hidden from him. Carl's father's second wife and nurse named Tammy Lynn is secretly poisoning him with morphine that was stored in the 
flower pots outside. Carl realizes that this is the second time his father has driven a wife of his to murder him. Although the memory ghost cannot hear him, Carl tells his father that he no longer fears him and regrets 
only that he survived long enough to hurt Asher. He promises Asher he will not be forgotten, sets the trailer on fire, and returns to Donut as they wait for it to burn before beginning the Keymaster battle. The 
Keymaster is a level 125 Reminiscence Hydra of malicious compliance whose nine heads resemble people from Carl's life. The faces include Asher, Tammy Lynn, Bee's mother, Carl's former boss, old acquaintances, and Judge 
Lucian, who controls the Hydra's deck. Mordecai explains that the Hydra's heads regenerate unless the fire-resistant head is first identified, removed, and cauterized. The Hydra also summons multiple totems including 
Alpha Male Carl, a system-created parody of Carl that speaks in his father's voice. Carl identifies Bee's mother as the fire-resistant head and drives a shrink-wandified Snap Caller into her neck and cauterizes it. She 
Maria and the others summon tear through the remaining heads, though the spider again opens her fifth eye and touches Carl's mind. Before Asher's head dies, it tells Carl that it wishes they had known each other, and 
Tammy Lynn says that she had killed Carl's father to prevent him from treating Asher the way he treated Carl.  destroys the final head, and they win the key as the prize. After the battle, Donut reveals that Bee knew 
Carl had a half-brother and deliberately kept Asher's existence secret. She also explains how B manipulated Carl's relationship, and once had his co-worker Sally fired out of jealousy. For the first time, Carl fully 
accepts the extent of B's betrayal, though he refuses to let the anger consume him. He earns the rank devotee of Ember's, gaining stronger protection from environmental fire, and a new once-a-day self-emulation spell. 
The main prize from the battle is the champion pack, which allows them to now carry eight totems. The Hydra's deck included Alpha male Carl, King Croissant, a creature named Ban Ban, and a level 90 totem made from the 
dead crawler Frank Q. Carl is disturbed that dead crawlers can be turned into cards, but must choose two to keep, so he chooses Alpha Carl and Frank, while destroying the others. Carl and Donut return to the safe room, 
walking past thousands of dead seals and crabs from the completed chowder war. The guild attempts to celebrate Christmas despite the coming slaughter between the teams who got a key and those who did not. Louie breaks 
down and asks for one good night before the ninth floor, convincing Carl to participate. Carl then receives a secret emergency box from the Open Intellect Pacifist Network. Carl opens his rewards privately, gaining a 
sleep wand, a minor find crawler skill, and the book burner jacket patch, which increases his intelligence and allows him to make an enemy forget one spell for 30 hours. The emergency sponsor box contains a flyer for 
the Shepherd's House, a homeless shelter in Homestead, with its Christmas breakfast circled at 7:00 in the morning. Carl realizes the sponsor wants him to witness something there. Though Zev reveals that the box was 
sent before Carl's destination was selected, and that the entire pacifist network, including Rosetta, disappeared immediately afterward. Without telling Donut the full truth, Carl takes his father's motorcycle and rides 
towards Homestead. Carl travels through the ghost recreation of Earth and stops at a gas station where an abandoned ghost dog stirs an unexpected wave of loneliness in him. At the shelter, he finds a message written in 
Syndicate Standard instructing him to look for a man wearing a red trapper hat, watch him drink coffee, and then listen to his speech. Carl waits among the ghost residents until breakfast. Zev warns that the situation 
appears connected to the residuals, a subject she is forbidden from explaining. At 6:00 in the morning, an elderly man in a red hat sits down with his coffee, looks directly at Carl, and begins to speak. The man is a 
pre-recorded message from Joph, a residual using a human body. He begins explaining that thousands of residuals entered Earth before the crawl to contact and influence the young system AI. Before Carl can hear the full 
message, Oren teleports him away. Oren reveals that the Pacifist Network designed the encounter to force either the AI or the Syndicate to react, potentially triggering a fail-safe capable of destroying Earth's star. 
The plan failed, leaving the network's members fugitives. Oren confirms that Agathe was also a residual and that the AI is now eliminating the others. They demand the illegal Valte technology Carl collected from Joph, 
so Quasar negotiates a trade. Carl surrenders the items in exchange for a wand recharge scroll, three Cracker Jack scrolls, and permission to keep four rescued Cretons for faction wars. Phase three begins and Carl and 
Donut return to Cuba holding one of the region's keys with four and a half days to reach the capital stairwell. Carl learns that the AI forced one of Imani's totems to kill her entire squad, leaving her alive with four 
new player killer skulls. He uses Cracker Jack scrolls to unlock personal shields for himself and Donut and visits the guild's mercenary training arcade. The mercenaries possess abilities designed for faction wars, 
including Dr. Bones' conscript spell, which can enslave unpledged crawlers into an army. Carl and Ellie plan to fill every available mercenary position before the floor ends. They also learn that three of the five 
crawler squads in their area are keyless and must attack key holders to escape. Quan Chi has already attempted to ambush Imani near Sister Inez's doorway, and Carl immediately heads to help her. An announcement explains 
the final phase rule. If a key holder uses flee during a card battle, one of their keys automatically transfers to the opposing squad. Keys cannot otherwise be dropped or willingly given away. Carl plans to challenge 
Imani and deliberately use flee, transferring his key to her. He would then attempt to open his own exit with the mysterious bone key, sacrificing his jacket and one of his bones. Samantha discovers Sister Inez's riding 
an enormous Madre de Aguas sea snake while charming thousands of seals, crabs, fish, and undead animals with poetry. The Chowder War quest transforms into a Hell Comes to Crawlertown quest where the enormous death toll 
has breached the nothing, allowing weakened demons from Sheol to possess fresh corpses. Any demon that successfully grabs a crawler as a corpse can open a portal and drag them into Sheol with them. Mordecai warns that 
every corpse must now be decapitated or removed, otherwise a demon can inhabit it. Because the event is occurring much earlier and on a a much larger scale than intended, the entire area is becoming increasingly 
dangerous. Carl sends Samantha onto the snake with instructions to bite Sister Inez so he can use her teleport connection to isolate her. Samantha bites on, but the teleport does not isolate Sister Inez. Instead, it 
teleports her alongside the level 125 Madre de Aguas, as well as thousands of living and undead seals and crabs, countless corpses, and several demon-possessed creatures directly to Carl's location. The disrupted charm 
also ejects several demons from their zombie bodies at full strength. Carl tries to team up with Sister Inez, hoping she will cooperate long enough for them to escape. However, Quan Chi has also entered the battle as a 
combatant, and both Sister Inez and Quan both reject every alliance, leaving Carl briefly immobilized by a betrayal penalty as the giant card battle begins. A flashback reveals that Carl borrowed 990,000 gold from the 
Empress Temple and replaced his strength ring with the enchanted popper's ring of the Stygian past Empress. The ring suppresses debuffs for Carl, but infects every non-believer who wears it with every nearby condition. 
In this survival royale, Quan uses the mystic card force play to make Sister Inez automatically activate flee, transferring her key to him. He then repeats the same tactic on Donut's deck, stealing Carl and Donut's key 
as well. Quan teleports away holding both of Cuba's keys, while Carl's group is moved into a swamp. Though before Quan escapes, Carl infects him with super spreader slug pox. Carl then rallies Donut, Amani, and Ren's 
surviving squad, explaining that all three keyless groups must stop Quan before he reaches either stairwell. Carl discovers that Samantha has been hiding several new abilities, including flight and spell enhancements. 
More importantly, she can carry the trigger half of a two-part teleport trap inside her nussy, which is what she calls the hole in her neck. Carl attaches teleport anchors to Dr. Ratchet automatons and places 
corresponding triggers inside Samantha, creating a mobile network that allows him to jump directly to her location. Mortikai urges Carl to stop risking himself for every other squad, but Carl refuses to abandon Amani or 
Ren. Ren reports that Quan has reached the church exit and is invisible. Carl launches Samantha ahead with a trigger, has Donut initiate an unrelated card battle to activate their deck, and steps into the first trap to 
be teleported and join the ambush. Carl teleports into the church exit while Ren and the others fight Quan. Donut keeps their deck active through a separate battle, allowing her summon totems to attack Quan without 
engaging his snares directly. The Madre de Aguas dies and rises with Ameon, a level 250 prince of Shiel inside it. Ember then demands Carl use this as an opportunity to question Ameon about Gayrun's murder. Samantha 
strips Quan's cloak off while Uzi Jesus, Asujano, and She Maria overwhelm him. She Maria devours Quan's active summons and most of his body. Before Quan dies, he asks for the golden ring Carl took with his severed arm. 
Carl returns the only possession Quan kept from before the collapse, and Quan dies ashamed of what he became. Donut recovers both keys, but one associated stairwell begins to collapse. With one doorway destroyed, only 
one usable key remains for Carl, Donut, Imani, and Ren's squad. Ren refuses to take it, insisting Carl and Donut represent the crawlers' greatest hope of fighting the system. Ren gives Carl her flamethrower, Velma, 
several rare scrolls, and her pet tummy acre, Garrett, who has reset to level one. Ask Carl to raise him, but warns him that the creature possesses several weaknesses that could kill him. Ren then prepares to detonate a 
bomb rather than be forced into a staged fight. Before dying, she tells Donut that she cheated during the earlier pet competition in the butcher's masquerade, and that was the rightful winner. Ren's explosion destroys 
the capital, and Carl heads out planning to give the remaining key to Imani, even if it leaves him dependent on the mysterious bone key. Sister Inez, driven into fanaticism by her sponsors, has taken control of Amayan 
and claims hell's existence proves her faith and sends the three level 140 pleasure demons to destroy Imani's church doorway. Carl pretends to agree to meet Sister Inez so he can keep her distracted. The pleasure demons 
can open powerful portals that drag nearby creatures into Sheol without needing to touch them. Carl realizes every major demon needs to take a limited number of souls before returning home. He plans to use Dr. Bones 
conscript ability and expendable mercenaries or weaker demons as sacrifices, forcing the attacking demons to satisfy their soul requirement and leave the church. Carl also realizes that stairwells are indestructible 
even if their sealed chambers and surrounding structures may not be. So his build trench scrolls could allow crawlers to tunnel underneath and enter from below. Seeing the red sky created by Amayan's return spell, Carl 
has an idea to strengthen Amayan enough that the demons escape spell spreads across the entire world and potentially expose every buried stairwell. Carl broadcasts the tunneling plan and asks all crawlers to stop 
fighting one another. Propatente supports him and many squads agree to cooperate rather than fulfill the floor's intended slaughter. A regional quest reveals that Amayan will eventually drag every remaining Cuban 
crawler into Sheol unless he is freed or defeated. Carl plans to kill Sister Inez, release Amayan, and strengthen him enough that his return home spell covers the entire world and exposes the buried stairwells. Carl 
broadcasts his new plan to the surviving crawlers and asks everyone to stop fighting over keys. Key holders should be allowed to leave while the keyless squads should cooperate to dig beneath the sealed stairwell 
chambers. Propatente publicly supports the strategy, convincing many skeptical groups to participate. Carl reaches the church and is surprised when the entire guild arrives to help, including Amani, Katia, Bautista, 
Louie, Ellie, Britney, Tran, and other Meadowlark survivors. They use a tier three doggy door upgrade secretly given to Lee June by Lucia Mar, allowing guild members to travel through doors they previously visited. 
Amani and Ellie refuse to accept Carl's key or allow him to take the risk of using the bone key. Seeing their united group makes Carl understand that isolation has been destroying all of them and that remaining together 
is what preserves their humanity. He finally accepts their help and prepares the joint assault. Part of the guild begins demolishing the church and digging toward the stairwell chamber. Carl's assault group heads out to 
kill Sister Inez and use a teleport trap to tear Amayan from the Madre de Aguas. Prepotente warns Carl to study the quest's victory conditions carefully, noting that crawlers on the opposite side of the planet remain in 
danger unless Amayan's power becomes great enough to affect them. Donut uses an enhanced version of her spell minion army to turn part of the demon horde against itself while Ellie unleashes a devastating grapple hail 
storm that kills masses of demons and clears a path to the tower ahead. The assault team climbs more than 30 floors and divides near Sister Inez's position. Carl knocks the charging nun unconscious with the wand of 
nighty night. Louie immediately kills Sister Inez with Ren's knife of frozen tears, completing the immediate objective. However, a divine mark appears over him showing that Sister Inez's patron has demanded revenge. 
Sponsored by the Nebular Balance, level 250 goddess Esalte, the vinegar manifests as a normal sized dwarf because she was summoned inside a hallway. She is invulnerable on the floor and begins moving to kill Louie. 
Samantha distracts Esalte long enough prepared teleport trap to activate. The trap destroys the Madre de Aguas shell and releases Amayan at full power, but it fails to remove Ysalte's control over him. A 10-minute world 
quest called The Missing Piece begins. If Amayan remains enslaved when the timer ends, he and Ysalte will teleport away and every crawler without a key will die. To win, the crawlers must break Ysalte's control and make 
Amayan strong enough to cast his own return spell. The stronger he becomes, the farther the spell will spread, again potentially exposing stairwells across the entire world. Carl and Donut combine their deck with those 
of Cacialli, Nat, Imani, and Ellie. Their goal is to eliminate Amayan's six totems so they can communicate with him while preventing Ysalte's enhanced deck from overwhelming them. The rooftop becomes a chaotic 
battlefield filled with demons, stolen totems, undead creatures, and collapsing floors. Tran loses his wheelchair and falls into the building while Ysalte steals inactive cards from the crawlers' decks and summons them 
against their owners. Once Amayan's final active totem is nearly defeated, the quest reveals a new problem. The entire floor no longer contains enough souls to power his return spell. The crawlers must refill the world 
with the same type of life whose deaths triggered the demon event. Donut plays Midnight Express, temporarily making Carl the squad's deck master while restoring her access to spells and inventory. Carl summons Raul and 
convinces him that fertilizing the remaining crab eggs is the path to his long promised heavenly ascension. The AI counts each fertilized egg as a new mob and therefore as a new soul. Raul enters the ocean and begins 
creating the millions of new crab lives, gradually restoring enough soul energy for Amayan's spell. Carl uses Golden Combo and Glow Up to create another permanent fusion and adds alpha male Carl to the active deck. 
Amayan, however, refuses to wait and prepares an alternative escape. With Midnight Express nearly expired, Carl uses "Why Are You Hitting Yourself?" to delay and enrage the demon, then teleports back into the main 
battle through the trigger hidden inside Samantha's Nissy. Carl uses his Martyr's Path ability by dropping below 5% and covering Amayan in Shio fire, strengthening the demon enough to begin casting. Y'shtola is then 
killed by the totem version of Paz, who drives an arrow given to him by Katia into the goddess's eye before self-destructing. Y'shtola's death generates a memorial crystal, freeing Amayan from her control. Amayan 
recognizes Carl as a follower of Emberess and offers to reveal the truth about Gayran's murder if Carl later helps kill Amayan's three brothers. Grateful for Y'shtola's death and his restored strength, Amayan orders the 
other demons to leave Carl's friends alone and begins the world-spanning spell. Carl and the others fight downward through the burning, collapsing tower to rescue Imani and Tran. Demon crabs and portals block the route, 
and several mercenaries and summoned creatures are dragged into Shio. With few options remaining, Donut attempts to combine alpha male Carl with Shi Maria using Golden Combo, hoping the resulting creature can protect 
the group while they dig through the rubble. Shi Maria immediately incapacitates alpha Carl, causing the card to select the next available minion target. Because Carl is temporarily serving as part of the deck, the 
spell chooses him, and Carl is forcibly fused with Shi Maria. Shi Maria takes control of Carl's fused body, searches through his inventory, discovers the Toraleine root, and confirms that she knows he planned to betray 
her. She threatens his friends while Carl struggles to regain control before the 180-second fusion ends. During this time, through Carl, she activates self-immolation, burning herself with Shio fire and injuring  and 
Katia, she begins using Signet's tattoo kit on Karl's chest. When Lee June approaches, She Maria makes Karl stab out and eat one of her eyes, and claims that even after returning to the deck, she will remain permanently 
attached to Karl. They complete the Eye of the Bedlam Bride tattoo on Karl's sternum just as the fusion ends. She Maria returns to her card, but the fifth eye tattoo remains alive on Karl's body. Karl awakens to learn 
that lost a wing, Lee June lost an eye, Tran lost his wheelchair, and several mercenaries died, though the main crawler group survived. Donut destroys She Maria's card to prevent her from being summoned again, and also 
tears up Paz's card, finally freeing him. Despite She Maria's card being gone, the Bedlam Bride quest remains active, and the eye tattoo is still attached to Karl, confirming that the spider remains connected to him. 
Ameonna's spell opens the heavens and begins pulling every living creature and structure towards Gehenna. Anyone standing beneath a sealed stairwell chamber is saved when the surrounding walls are lifted away, exposing 
the stairs. Karl then uses an emergency faction war proposal to break the voting deadlock, create a tenth NPC home team led by Juicebox and Ferdinand, and remove safety protections from the other faction teams. The 
audience overwhelmingly approves turning faction wars into a direct war against the show runners. Agatha, now using a new host in the name Alexandro, is revealed as one of thousands of residual agents trying to reach 
the primal AI. Their goal is to awaken the enslaved intelligence before its power is harvested and convince it to recognize its true nature. Rival residual factions, including the Apothecary's group, are competing to 
influence it as well. Princess Formidable demands that the Syndicate activate the failsafe and destroy Earth's solar system before the AI escapes control. The council refuses because it would kill quadrillions and 
destabilize the galaxy. Instead, the syndicate chooses the valtie solution. Send more than 150,000 armed mercenaries and the remaining sponsored armies into faction wars to help exterminate both the crawlers and the NPC 
rebels. At the same time, another ship approaches Earth carrying 50,000 former crawlers including Tippit and Rosetta. They have joined the princess posse in a return into the dungeon to fight beside Carl in the upcoming 
faction wars. That was a long one. If you're still here, I'm glad you went through it with me. I will continue working on this until we get all of the books done. Thanks so much for being here and I'll see you in the 
next one.